        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/b5ac83/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-06-06T00:47:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I frequently play Twilight Imperium, with expansions. I suppose my favorite rule in Sentinels, which prevents arguments, is that players adjucate ambiguity. TI doesn't have that, and instead has like a pretty long faq/errata, but it's far from comprehensive, and sometimes the rules arguments get... lengthy. (Actually had like a 2 hour discussion last night about something... it sucked.)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Oh, and I was just poking fun Spiff, I use your FAQ often, as well as your other resources. I actually regret not having my laptop handy when I was showing the game to some new people, I forgot how easy Gloomy is when not playing with his \"Gloomier\" version.</p>",
